{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs GNU C++11 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following GNU C++11 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nToday is the final contest of INOI (Iranian National Olympiad in Informatics). The contest room is a row with $$$n$$$ computers. All computers are numbered with integers from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$ from left to right. There are $$$m$$$ participants, numbered with integers from $$$1$$$ to $$$m$$$.We have an array $$$a$$$ of length $$$m$$$ where $$$a_{i}$$$ ($$$1 \\leq a_i \\leq n$$$) is the computer behind which the $$$i$$$-th participant wants to sit.Also, we have another array $$$b$$$ of length $$$m$$$ consisting of characters 'L' and 'R'. $$$b_i$$$ is the side from which the $$$i$$$-th participant enters the room. 'L' means the participant enters from the left of computer $$$1$$$ and goes from left to right, and 'R' means the participant enters from the right of computer $$$n$$$ and goes from right to left.The participants in the order from $$$1$$$ to $$$m$$$ enter the room one by one. The $$$i$$$-th of them enters the contest room in the direction $$$b_i$$$ and goes to sit behind the $$$a_i$$$-th computer. If it is occupied he keeps walking in his direction until he reaches the first unoccupied computer. After that, he sits behind it. If he doesn't find any computer he gets upset and gives up on the contest.The madness of the $$$i$$$-th participant is the distance between his assigned computer ($$$a_i$$$) and the computer he ends up sitting behind. The distance between computers $$$i$$$ and $$$j$$$ is equal to $$$|i - j|$$$.The values in the array $$$a$$$ can be equal. There exist $$$n^m \\cdot 2^m$$$ possible pairs of arrays $$$(a, b)$$$.Consider all pairs of arrays $$$(a, b)$$$ such that no person becomes upset. For each of them let's calculate the sum of participants madnesses. Find the sum of all these values.You will be given some prime modulo $$$p$$$. Find this sum by modulo $$$p$$$.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the GNU C++11 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\n#include<bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n#define int long long\nconst int N=507;\nint n,m,p,fac[N],ifac[N],f[N][N],g[N][N],ans[N][N],sum[N][N];\ninline int pows(long long u,int v){\n\tlong long ans=1;\n\twhile(v>0){\n\t\tif(v&1) ans=ans*u%p; u=u*u%p,v=v>>1;\n\t}\n\treturn ans;\n}\ninline long long binom(int a,int b){\n\tif(a<b) return 0; return 1ll*fac[a]%p*ifac[b]%p*ifac[a-b]%p;\n}\ninline int getsum(int u){\n\treturn 1ll*u*(u+1)/2;\n} \nsigned main(){\n\tcin>>n>>m>>p,fac[0]=ifac[0]=1;\n\tfor(int i=1;i<=500;i++) fac[i]=1ll*fac[i-1]*i%p,ifac[i]=pows(fac[i],p-2);\n\tfor(int len=1;len<=n;len++)\n\t\tfor(int l=1;l<=n;l++)\n\t\tfor(int r=l;r<=n;r++){\n\t\t\tif(r-l+1!=len) continue;\n\t\t\tif(l==r){\n\t\t\t\tf[l][r]=0,g[l][r]=2;\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\telse{\n\t\t\t\tg[l][r]=2ll*(g[l+1][r]+g[l][r-1])%p;\n\t\t\t\tfor(int x=l+1;x<=r;x++){\n\t\t\t\t\tf[l][r]=(f[l][r]+1ll*f[l+1][r]+1ll*g[l+1][r]*(x-l))%p;\n\t\t\t\t\tg[l][r]=(g[l][r]+g[l+1][r])%p;\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\tfor(int x=l;x<=r-1;x++){\n\t\t\t\t\tf[l][r]=(f[l][r]+1ll*f[l][r-1]+1ll*g[l][r-1]*(r-x))%p;\n\t\t\t\t\tg[l][r]=(g[l][r]+g[l][r-1])%p;\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\tf[l][r]=(f[l][r]+f[l+1][r]*2ll+f[l][r-1]*2ll)%p;\n\t\t\t\tfor(int x=l+1;x<=r-1;x++){\n\t\t\t\t\tf[l][r]=(f[l][r]+1ll*(1ll*f[l][x-1]*g[x+1][r]%p+1ll*f[x+1][r]*g[l][x-1]%p)*(r-l+2)%p*binom(r-l,x-l))%p;\n\t\t\t\t\tf[l][r]=(f[l][r]+1ll*(getsum(x-l)+getsum(r-x))*g[x+1][r]%p*g[l][x-1]%p*binom(r-l,x-l))%p;\n\t\t\t\t\tg[l][r]=(g[l][r]+1ll*g[x+1][r]%p*g[l][x-1]%p*binom(r-l,x-l)%p*(r-l+2))%p;\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\tans[0][0]=0,sum[0][0]=1;\n\tfor(int i=1;i<=n;i++){\n\t\tfor(int j=i;j<=n;j++)\n\t\t\tfor(int k=0;k<=n;k++){\n\t\t\t\tint t=k+j-i+1; if(t>m) continue;\n\t\t\t\tans[j+1][t]=(ans[j+1][t]+1ll*ans[i-1][k]*g[i][j]%p*binom(t,j-i+1))%p;\n\t\t\t\tans[j+1][t]=(ans[j+1][t]+1ll*f[i][j]*sum[i-1][k]%p*binom(t,j-i+1))%p;\n\t\t\t\tsum[j+1][t]=(sum[j+1][t]+1ll*g[i][j]*sum[i-1][k]%p*binom(t,j-i+1))%p;\n\t\t\t}\n\t\tfor(int j=0;j<=n;j++){\n\t\t\tans[i][j]=(ans[i][j]+ans[i-1][j])%p;\n\t\t\tsum[i][j]=(sum[i][j]+sum[i-1][j])%p;\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tcout<<(ans[n+1][m]+ans[n][m])%p<<endl;\n}\n//3 2 998244353\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n#define int long long\n\nconst int N = 507;\n\nint n, m, p;\nint fac[N], ifac[N];\nint f[N][N], g[N][N];\nint dp[N][N], sum_dp[N][N];\n\ninline int pows(long long u, int v) {\n    long long ans = 1;\n    while (v > 0) {\n        if (v & 1) ans = ans * u % p;\n        u = u * u % p;\n        v >>= 1;\n    }\n    return ans;\n}\n\ninline int binom(int a, int b) {\n    if (a < b) return 0;\n    return 1ll * fac[a] % p * ifac[b] % p * ifac[a - b] % p;\n}\n\ninline int getsum(int u) {\n    return u * (u + 1) / 2;\n}\n\nsigned main() {\n    cin >> n >> m >> p;\n    fac[0] = ifac[0] = 1;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= 500; i++) {\n        fac[i] = 1ll * fac[i - 1] * i % p;\n        ifac[i] = pows(fac[i], p - 2);\n    }\n\n    // Initialize DP for intervals\n    for (int len = 1; len <= n; len++) {\n        for (int l = 1; l <= n; l++) {\n            int r = l + len - 1;\n            if (r > n) continue;\n\n            if (l == r) {\n                f[l][r] = 0;\n                g[l][r] = 2; // Two ways: L and R\n            } else {\n                // Case 1: First person sits at position l (enters from left)\n                f[l][r] = (f[l][r] + f[l + 1][r] + g[l + 1][r] * (l - l)) % p;\n                g[l][r] = (g[l][r] + g[l + 1][r]) % p;\n\n                // Case 2: First person sits at position r (enters from right)\n                f[l][r] = (f[l][r] + f[l][r - 1] + g[l][r - 1] * (r - r)) % p;\n                g[l][r] = (g[l][r] + g[l][r - 1]) % p;\n\n                // Case 3: First person sits at position x (l < x < r)\n                for (int x = l + 1; x < r; x++) {\n                    // Left part: [l, x-1], Right part: [x+1, r]\n                    int left_len = x - l;\n                    int right_len = r - x;\n                    int total_len = r - l;\n\n                    // The first person sits at x\n                    // Left participants: choose left_len positions from total_len\n                    // Right participants: choose right_len positions from total_len\n\n                    // Contribution from left and right parts\n                    f[l][r] = (f[l][r] + \n                               f[l][x - 1] * g[x + 1][r] % p +\n                               f[x + 1][r] * g[l][x - 1] % p) % p;\n\n                    // Contribution from the distance for the first person\n                    f[l][r] = (f[l][r] + \n                               (getsum(left_len) + getsum(right_len)) % p * \n                               g[l][x - 1] % p * g[x + 1][r] % p) % p;\n\n                    // Total ways\n                    g[l][r] = (g[l][r] + \n                               g[l][x - 1] * g[x + 1][r] % p * binom(total_len, left_len) % p) % p;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    // DP for the whole problem\n    dp[0][0] = 0;\n    sum_dp[0][0] = 1;\n\n    for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {\n        for (int j = i; j <= n; j++) {\n            int len = j - i + 1;\n            for (int k = 0; k <= m; k++) {\n                if (k + len > m) continue;\n                \n                // Add contribution of interval [i, j]\n                dp[j][k + len] = (dp[j][k + len] + \n                                  dp[i - 1][k] * g[i][j] % p * binom(k + len, len) % p +\n                                  sum_dp[i - 1][k] * f[i][j] % p * binom(k + len, len) % p) % p;\n                \n                sum_dp[j][k + len] = (sum_dp[j][k + len] + \n                                      sum_dp[i - 1][k] * g[i][j] % p * binom(k + len, len) % p) % p;\n            }\n        }\n        \n        // Prefix sums\n        for (int k = 0; k <= m; k++) {\n            dp[i][k] = (dp[i][k] + dp[i - 1][k]) % p;\n            sum_dp[i][k] = (sum_dp[i][k] + sum_dp[i - 1][k]) % p;\n        }\n    }\n\n    cout << (dp[n][m] + sum_dp[n][m]) % p << endl;\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.3\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-4.0531076592742465e-06, -0.0004015354788862169, -3.814689989667386e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -2.729855441430118e-05, -0.20209231972694397, -0.0009448830969631672, -2.622600959512056e-06, -5.602820692729438e-06, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -1.7046782886609435e-05, -4.529942543740617e-06, -3.2186455882765586e-06, -0.10020776838064194, -0.732288658618927, -0.06052318960428238, -2.8967437174287625e-05, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.04304935410618782, -0.012568551115691662, -1.9311717551317997e-05, -0.8698402047157288, -0.0004968600696884096, 0.0, -0.0037311953492462635, -0.007724178954958916, -0.0015036477707326412, -0.31326985359191895, -0.0006542449118569493, -7.70062324590981e-05, -3.933898824470816e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -5.960462772236497e-07, -0.04056797921657562, -0.012855512090027332, -0.004111884627491236, -0.057121314108371735, -4.768360213347478e-06, -7.152531907195225e-06, -0.000311445357